{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"Strategy: treat the two `Iff`s as equivalences between propositions that are each independently true; no implication between their mathematical contents is needed.\n\n- For the first `Iff`:\n  - `cardDistinctFactors n` is the cardinality of the support of the prime factorization. Its value is `1` exactly when that support is a singleton, equivalently when `n` is a positive prime power. This is `ArithmeticFunction.cardDistinctFactors_eq_one_iff`.\n  - If `l` is squarefree, then `l = ∏ p ∈ l.primeFactors, p`. The primes are pairwise coprime, so repeated use of multiplicativity gives `f l = ∏ p ∈ l.primeFactors, f p`; use `ArithmeticFunction.IsMultiplicative.prod_primeFactors`. [Relevant arithmetic-function results](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/master/Mathlib/NumberTheory/ArithmeticFunction/Misc.lean)\n\n- For the second `Iff`:\n  - A unit has an empty factor multiset, hence its UFD Möbius value is `(-1)^0 = 1`; this is exactly `IsUnit.moebius_eq`. [UFD Möbius documentation](https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/RingTheory/UniqueFactorizationDomain/Moebius.html)\n  - The identity `μ * log = Λ` is Möbius inversion applied to `Λ * ζ = log`, where `*` is Dirichlet convolution. After coercing the integer-valued Möbius function to real values, use `ArithmeticFunction.moebius_mul_log_eq_vonMangoldt`. [Von Mangoldt identities](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/master/Mathlib/NumberTheory/ArithmeticFunction/VonMangoldt.lean)\n\nThus split the outer conjunction and each equivalence, and in every direction ignore the hypothesis and establish the target from its corresponding library theorem. The squarefree assumption is essential in the prime-factor product formula: otherwise multiplicities are absent from `primeFactors`."}}
